   "id": "co_wham_ridge",
   "area_id": "co_vestal_peak",
   "name": "Wham Ridge",
   "grade": "5.4",
   "discipline": "alpine",
   "overview": "Vestal's north face, with plenty of line choices. Hike the low-angle lower section to a big grassy ledge slanting up right, or to the boulder-covered ledge about 2.5 pitches above, and tie in there. Pitches 1 to 4 are quite easy, and the face then steepens. Pitches 5 and 6 are the crux zone (maybe 5.5) as smooth low-angle rock turns to steeper, chunkier ground. Pitches 7 to 9 climb a bowl with stepped ledges to a false summit, then a trail heads south and up. Pitches are full 60 meter ropelengths. Roping up all the way is optional, though exposure persists.",
